# Execution log: fifth project parity review remediation

## Start
- Created branch `fix/parity-fifth-review-2026-10-28` from clean revision `dbbabeb0`.
- Read both supplied review plan files and the ignored evidence bundle. Scope is I02 bounded/cancellation-safe shutdown, I03 encoding-failure isolation, and I01 current callback group attribution.
- Evidence remains under ignored `/evidence/`; it will not be staged or committed.
- No repository-local `AGENTS.md` applies. Coding workflow requires phase commits, validation, and a full-plan final audit.


## I02 — bounded, cancellation-safe dispatcher shutdown
- Updated producer and Lite trace dispatchers to stop accepting appends atomically with shutdown, and move draining/cleanup into a shared supervisor task that survives cancellation of a caller.
- Applied a single five-second drain deadline and a five-second producer-cleanup deadline; after the drain deadline the worker is aborted and joined, then the owned trace producer is unregistered and stopped. Fixed the worker-start failure cleanup path and added a Push consumer owner shutdown regression test.
- Added full-queue and cancelled-caller tests for both dispatchers. Focused tests passed: producer `trace::tests` (10), Lite `lite::trace::tests` (9), and Push owner shutdown (1). Full workspace and integration gates are recorded below after all phases.

## I03 — isolate malformed trace encoding failures
- Wrapped each `TraceContext::encode` call at the batch boundary with panic isolation. An invalid context is logged and skipped while later valid contexts in the same batch remain eligible for delivery; public encoding semantics are unchanged.
- Added a mixed malformed/valid unit test covering invalid SubAfter, Pub, and EndTransaction contexts followed by a valid Recall row. The focused producer trace test suite passed (10 tests), and the loopback evidence probe confirmed that valid records still send after malformed records.

## I02 committed-boundary completion
- Final commit review found the producer dispatcher import, flush rejection, and worker-owned shutdown integration still unstaged in the phase commit; completed those hunks in follow-up commit 3314237b. The final committed tree was then rebuilt and all workspace checks passed.

## I01 — use callback-time producer group
- Removed startup-time group capture from both producer hooks. Pub captures the callback context group before send and retains it for the paired after hook; EndTransaction reads its own callback context. Both paths remove one namespace prefix and preserve a nullable group.
- Added regression coverage for a changed/nested group, hook mutation between callbacks, actual trace sends, independent business send group, and null callback groups.

